    "body": "closes #30258\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`nvim_del_keymap()`, `nvim_buf_del_keymap()` and `vim.keymap.del()` match a\r\nmapping by its `{rhs}` as well as its `{lhs}` in a two-round scan if no detected mapping is found.\r\n\r\n so deleting one `{lhs}` can wipe an unrelated mapping. that contradicts the documented removal by `{lhs}`.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nas clason suggested, just change the lua api contract. namely, route the API unmap path through the existing `MAPTYPE_UNMAP_LHS` so only `{lhs}` is matched\r\n\r\nleave `:unmap` alone for compatibility.",
    "closed_at": null,
